LEETCODE__974. Subarray Sums Divisible by K
Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return the number of non-empty subarrays that have a sum divisible by k.
A subarray is a contiguous part of an array.

Example 1:
Input: nums = [4,5,0,-2,-3,1], k = 5
Output: 7
Explanation: There are 7 subarrays with a sum divisible by k = 5:
[4, 5, 0, -2, -3, 1], [5], [5, 0], [5, 0, -2, -3], [0], [0, -2, -3], [-2, -3]
Example 2:
Input: nums = [5], k = 9
Output: 0
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Interview Recall Bullet Points:

• Use prefix sum modulo pattern
• Same modulo → divisible subarray
• Normalize modulo for negatives
• Use HashMap to count frequency
• Use nC2 formula to count subarrays
• O(N) optimal solution
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIMAL SOLUTION:TIME COMPLEXITY:O(N) AND SPACE COMPLEXITY:O(N)
class Solution {
    public int subarraysDivByK(int[] nums, int k) {
        int prefixsum=0,result=0,modulo=0;
        Map<Integer,Integer> mapp=new HashMap<>();
        mapp.put(0,1);
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
        {
            prefixsum=prefixsum+nums[i];
            modulo = (prefixsum % k + k) % k;
            if(mapp.containsKey(modulo))
            {
                mapp.put(modulo,(mapp.get(modulo))+1);
            }
            else
            {
                mapp.put(modulo,1);
            }
        }
        for(Map.Entry<Integer,Integer> entry : mapp.entrySet())
        {
            int f=entry.getValue();
            result=result + (f*(f-1))/2;
        }
        return result;
    }
}
